                    "title": "May — There is / To have",
                    "type": "note",
                    "content": "'May' is one of the most useful words in Ilonggo. It expresses existence ('there is') and possession ('I have').\n\n• May tubig. → There is water.\n• May plete ako. → I have fare money.\n• May bata sila. → They have a child."
                }
